proxmod-example-hello (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop 'use strict' from the frontend asset. It breaks every callParent in
    the file: ExtJS resolves the parent method through Function.caller, which
    V8 reports as null for a strict-mode caller.

 -- proxmod maintainers <proxmod@localhost>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

proxmod-example-hello (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Demonstrate the config panel menu API: the extension now registers one
    menu screen and one menu section alongside its node tab, so both modes
    are exercised by something that ships.
  * Requires proxmod (>= 0.2.0) for that API.

